   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "No other option",
     "texto": [
      "**V-(으)ㄹ 수밖에 없다** expresses that, given the circumstances, there is no other option but to do something: 받다 → **받을 수밖에 없어요**, 기다리다 → **기다릴 수밖에 없어요**. **-을** is used after a consonant and **-ㄹ** after a vowel.",
      "오늘까지 신청해야 해서 지금 **제출할 수밖에 없어요** = I have to apply today, so there is no choice but to hand it in now."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "It does not mean general obligation",
     "texto": [
      "**-아/어야 하다** expresses an obligation or necessity; **-(으)ㄹ 수밖에 없다** stresses that the options are limited by the situation.",
      "막차가 끊겨서 택시를 **탈 수밖에 없었어요** = as there were no more buses, there was no choice but to take a taxi."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
